        "original_id": "3f9d6d26-b2d8-5fd6-b50c-d41d98890eb0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Phrases: \"Lest we forget\"\n- Events: Remembrance Day, ANZAC Day\n- Organizations: Australian and New Zealand Army Corps (ANZAC)\n- Places: Gallipoli\n- Countries: English-speaking countries, Australia, New Zealand, Ottoman Empire\n- Topics: war remembrance, World War I\n\nFacts:\n- ANZAC Day is observed on 25 April each year.\n- ANZAC Day was originally established to honour members of the Australian and New Zealand Army Corps (ANZAC).\n- Members of the Australian and New Zealand Army Corps fought at Gallipoli against the Ottoman Empire during World War I.\n- The phrase \"Lest we forget\" is commonly used in war remembrance services and commemorative occasions in English-speaking countries.\n- The phrase \"Lest we forget\" is used especially for Remembrance Day and ANZAC Day commemorations.",
